cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mariasol: an instrument for analysing European legislative negotiation"
abstract: >-
  Builds member state position maps, coalition structures and Council
  arithmetic from the primary documents of a European legislative negotiation,
  and reads amending acts ("omnibus") by parsing their modification
  instructions deterministically. Computation is deterministic; a language
  model is used only to qualify an already-established divergence, and every
  model-produced claim is discarded unless its quotation is located verbatim in
  the source corpus.
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
